// Control-only reset re-verification - 11/06/26
- The reset policy was changed to clear only FSM/valid state. W/B and output
  datapath clears were removed; timing, operand selection, and all latencies are unchanged.
- WSL Verilator reran the same seven configurations in the table above:
  2,495 completed transactions over 13,023 clocks, including 147 reset clocks.
- The golden control schedule and independent exact-arithmetic golden words were
  reused. The scoreboard preserves expected output data across reset and compares
  each word once it has received its first qualified write.
- Before first writes, data is unspecified. Hold checks use case equality, allowing
  unknown initial values rather than requiring zeros. Every output must retain its
  previous value on a clock without its qualified write, including reset clocks.
- W/B operand holding registers were also checked for unchanged contents on every
  reset edge. valid_o was checked every clock, including all reset/abort intervals.
- These checks verify that stale/retained data never becomes a valid completed
  bundle, all outputs have been written before a completion, and early A still
  updates with WiBi at T+L+2 while complete valid remains at T+L+4.
- Questa 2025.2 four-state compatibility smoke passed 359 transactions over
  1,835 clocks, including 21 reset clocks, with no initial-zero assumption and
  no compile/simulation errors or warnings.
- Updated evidence paths from repository root:
    simulate/fft_core_control_reset_checks/results.json
    simulate/fft_core_control_reset_checks/regression.log
    simulate/fft_core_control_reset_checks/<case>/verilator.log
    simulate/fft_core_control_reset_checks/<case>/vectors.txt
    simulate/fft_core_control_reset_checks/questa/smoke.log
